    "result_text": "The full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test, 0 failures).\n\n## Summary\n\nI added a derived, read-only `checkDigit` field to the owner response \u2014 the Luhn (mod 10) check digit over the digits of `customerCode` \u2014 following the codebase's existing derived-field pattern rather than adding storage or ad-hoc logic.\n\nThree focused changes, each in its natural home:\n\n1. **`util/Luhn.java`** (new) \u2014 a small, single-responsibility utility with a public static `checkDigit(String)` implementing the generic Luhn algorithm over the digit characters (non-digits ignored). Generic and reusable; lives in the existing `util` package rather than being buried in the mapper or the owner-specific code.\n\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 declared `checkDigit` (integer, `readOnly`, 0\u20139) right after `customerCode`, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field.\n\n3. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added `@Mapping(target = \"checkDigit\", expression = \"java(checkDigit(owner))\")` plus a `default Integer checkDigit(Owner owner)` that returns `null` when there's no owner/code and otherwise delegates to `Luhn.checkDigit(...)`. This mirrors the sibling `membershipNumber` derivation exactly, so both GET and POST responses (which share the mapper) include it.\n\nThe new `coreCheckDigitIsLuhnOfCustomerCode` test passes and the full suite builds green.",
